      <title>Federal government sends $200 million to Indiana to support rural healthcare</title>
      <link>https://www.ipm.org/news/2025-12-31/federal-government-sends-200-million-to-indiana-to-support-rural-healthcare</link>
      <description>Indiana to receive $200 million from federal government for rural healthcare. But health experts say those funds are unlikely to offset the estimated $137-billion cut to Medicaid spending in rural areas from Trump's tax and spending bill passed in July.</description>
